  clock: 3  # c091
  nonce: c091  # c091
  message: "Fixed in PR #2175 (dev, \"fix(sketch): byte-identical Additional Files are listed and printed once\", 2026-11-13). Candidates with the same bytes are folded into one before ranking (sketch._group_identical_files): the shallowest path stays, then the first by name; its copies are named beside it in the listing (\"same content: ...\") and above its content, the first three by name and the rest as a count; a README link to a copy counts for the file that stands for it. EVIDENCE, the filed instance (hypergumbo sketch . -t 128000 on the branch): \"- `README.md` (same content: `packages/hypergumbo/README.md`)\" appears once in the listing, the content section prints README.md once under \"*The same content is at `packages/hypergumbo/README.md`.*\", and the copy's path occurs twice in the whole sketch (those two notes) where it was a listed entry and a second 21 KB block. GENERALITY, measured on the 444-repository corpus (candidates as the sketch discovers them): 217 repositories have byte-identical candidates and 8,092 of 115,338 candidates (7.0%) fold; rolldown folds 992 of 2,283 (one config file has 106 copies), nextjs 640 of 2,750, gatekeeper 423 of 1,001, airflow 220 of 2,401 (70 copies of one .rst). The rule compares content, never names. THE NEAR-IDENTICAL QUESTION the item asked to be decided: same bytes, nothing else; a file that differs by a trailing newline is a different file; empty and unreadable files stand alone (each pinned by a test). Eight mutations each went red. NOT DONE: Source Files Content can still print two source files with the same bytes; the item named it as a place to apply the rule \"if that section can print two files with the same bytes\", and I did not measure how often it does."  # c091
